  "summary": "Hypnagogic pop is a loosely defined style of pop and psychedelic music that evokes cultural memory and nostalgia for the popular entertainment of the past. It emerged in the 2000s through a wave of American Millennial home recording artists in the lo-fi and post-noise scene, who adopted retro aesthetics from their childhood, such as radio and soft rock, new wave, video game music, synth-pop, R\u0026B and early Internet aesthetics. Recordings were typically marked by the use of outmoded analog equipment and DIY experimentation, while distributed on cassettes and CD-R's with circulation primarily based on the Internet through blog sites.",
